  "body": "Stacked on #805 (which stacks on #800). Fork synced at v0.17.0. Effort: medium\n\n## What changed\n- New MCP tools in `crates/app/src/mcp/holders.rs`: `set_tool_holder` (`tool` + exactly one of `library` [optional `gauge_len`, `projection`], `points` [`{z, r, arc}`], or `clear: true`) and `list_holder_library` (every entry, taper, clamp, default/min/max gauge length).\n- All modes go through `SetToolBody::library` / `::spun`: one call is one undo step; refusals (unknown entry, shank the holder can't take, both/neither of library/points/clear, empty or malformed profile, negative or non-finite mm, too-short gauge) are tool errors naming the reason.\n- `get_job` shows each tool's `holder` (`null` = plain cylinder).\n- camcraft-mcp skill tool table lists both tools; `PROCESS_VERSION` 10 -> 11 (skill edit).\n- No script verb (decision in `docs/decisions/799-mcp-set-tool-holder.md`).\n\n## Tests\n`crates/app/tests/mcp_holder.rs` (5): `library_entry_lands_on_the_tool_and_get_job_shows_it`, `undo_restores_the_previous_holder_in_one_step`, `drawn_points_set_and_clear_restores_the_cylinder`, `list_holder_library_names_every_entry_with_dimensions`, `bad_input_is_refused_by_name_and_changes_nothing`. Also green: `mcp` (13), `mcp_pockets` (3), `mcp_setup` (6); `clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Not exercised\nFull quick/batch gate, GUI, camcraft-tools suites (crate untouched), a real post/sim with a library holder via MCP.\n\nChangelog: `MCP set_tool_holder and list_holder_library: set a tool's holder from the built-in library, a drawn profile, or clear it; get_job shows each tool's holder`\n\nFixes #799\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
